Adds a separate canonical MTF 30/10/5 LONG↔SHORT strategy without changing or activating any current LIVE pilot.

Signal contract:
- FLAT + closed 5m CROSS_UP in 30m BULLISH/RECOVERING context -> provisional LONG;
- FLAT + closed 5m CROSS_DOWN in 30m BEARISH/DETERIORATING context -> provisional SHORT;
- closed 10m validates/rejects provisional legs;
- 5m/10m failures flatten only and never carry an opposite target;
- an opposite closed 30m cross is the sole full reversal signal.

Execution contract:
- LONG -> SHORT and SHORT -> LONG are always two-step: CLOSE -> confirmed Saxo FLAT -> OPEN opposite;
- no one-order reverse and no pyramiding;
- the closed-30m reversal intent is persisted across the asynchronous close/P&L reconciliation boundary;
- a newer closed 30m cross may supersede an uncompleted pending target, while 5m/10m clocks cannot;
- BOOTSTRAP_NO_REPLAY adopts actual Saxo exposure and historical/stale bars never replay orders;
- the strategy runtime has no Saxo POST authority and only emits ordinary execution requests;
- existing generic CLOSE and OPEN executors remain authoritative, including settled close/P&L provenance, direction-specific Product Admission, explicit NBP/limited-loss acknowledgement, current entry authority, pilot equity, Margin Envelope, final Saxo precheck, durable attempt-before-POST and uncertain-submit handling;
- both LONG and SHORT Product Admission are required before Full auto can be armed.

V1 intentionally fails closed if a newer 30m reversal supersedes a pending target while the old CLOSE has already crossed its durable submission boundary: ending FLAT is preferred to reconstructing an uncertain opposite exposure.

Activation remains explicit. This PR only makes `MTF 30/10/5 · long/short flip` selectable; it does not switch the currently configured MTF short/flat pilot.

Final branch CI: 1022 passed.

Follow-up after deep screening PR #42. Continued source-level screening found two additional runtime regressions plus one stale acceptance contract:

- the native Electron Explorer context menu still exposed `Add File/Folder to Chat`, which now always fails because provider pages are MANUAL_ONLY; the obsolete visible native action is removed;
- an IDLE/ERROR Preview or active Inspector could be expanded back over the shell by a later resize event; a post-resize guard now keeps native Preview collapsed unless Preview is active and state is LIVE/LOADING;
- `REAL_MAC_UI_ACCEPTANCE.md` still described the forbidden legacy provider-DOM injection flow; it is aligned with the Workspace Agent / Transaction Engine architecture and final Mac gate.

Regression coverage now explicitly prevents native Explorer chat actions, Preview resize resurrection, and acceptance-document reauthorization of provider DOM automation.

Fix du bloqueur observe en production: le timer de sollicitation PNJ etait recrée a chaque mise a jour de `npcs` (Living City tick ~18 s), donc le delai de 45 s pouvait ne jamais arriver a terme.

Changements:
- le timer n'est plus dependant du tableau `npcs` reactif;
- le candidat PNJ est resolu au moment ou le timer expire via `useGameStore.getState()`;
- retry toutes les 15 s si aucun candidat n'est disponible;
- route Map rendue plus robuste (`/map` ou suffixe `/map`);
- ajout d'un `testID` stable pour les futurs E2E;
- refus toujours neutre et cooldown conserve.

Gate: CI + Vercel verts avant merge.

