## Summary

Trim exact-disorder helper declarations that are not part of the reusable public physics boundary, and update the architecture contracts to match the reduced dependency graph.

- remove the unused `average_finiteDimensionalOperatorTrace` theorem from `Transport/Disorder/Finite.lean`;
- remove the now-unused `Analysis.Operator.FiniteTrace` import from `Finite.lean`;
- remove the stale `transportFiniteDisorder` required-import contract that existed to guard that former trace consumer;
- remove the corresponding `finiteTrace -> finiteDisorder` edge from the scoped source topology while retaining the real `finiteTrace -> stredaTraceKernel` edge;
- make `averagedGreen_injective` private in `AveragedSelfEnergy.lean`, since it is only an internal step toward the public `averagedGreen_isUnit` result;
- preserve `average_congr`, `operatorAverage_star`, `averagedGreen_isUnit`, `exactSelfEnergy`, and the exact self-energy existence/uniqueness API.

This follows the intent of #1768: finite trace is owned by `Analysis.Operator.FiniteTrace` and consumed only where an ordinary trace is genuinely required. Once the sole finite-disorder trace bridge is removed, keeping an otherwise-unused import or architecture edge would preserve a stale dependency rather than an architectural boundary. No new CI regression machinery is added.

