## Scope

Bounded test-only refinement of the merged F2 Hidden Exception fixture.

It verifies that the specific source-linked claim containing the later-task material (Hidden Exception X) is surfaced by the existing `GlobalDocumentSynthesis.unsupported_source_claim_ids` contract when that material is absent from the bounded T1 digest.

This distinguishes an existing representation-gap signal from unrelated truth/evidence `gap_notice` semantics.

## Proves

- the specific T2-material claim remains source-linked;
- it is omitted from the compact T1 digest;
- the existing synthesis contract exposes that exact omitted claim as unsupported;
- `source_claims_not_represented_in_synthesis` is emitted;
- `NOT REPRESENTED != ABSENT` can use an existing owner-local signal without adding a new production enum/module.

## Does not prove

- later-task reopen is implemented;
- durable Reader resume exists;
- `gap_notice` and representation insufficiency are the same concept;
- any new runtime, Canon, persistence, or Crystal authority.

## Merge evidence metadata

Documentation impact: GITHUB_ONLY

Disposition: `EXISTING CONTRACT REUSED + TEST EVIDENCE`; later-task reopen remains `NOT_ESTABLISHED`.

